{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"set -euo pipefail\ncat /Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/config/discussion_controls.json\nprintf '\\\\n---TOPIC---\\\\n'\ncat /Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/quantum-physics/topics/topic-special-purpose-platforms-for-near-term-quantum-learning.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"schema_version\": \"comment_section_discussion_controls_v1\",\n  \"defaults\": {},\n  \"pages\": {}\n}\n\n---TOPIC---\n{\n  \"claim_ids\": [\n    \"claim-deep-quantum-learning-can-use-quantum-annealers-programmable-photonic-circuits-a--0bdb973219c3\",\n    \"claim-quantum-boltzmann-machine-training-can-gain-quadratic-improvements-in-thermaliza--2d6a13e72831\",\n    \"claim-the-demonstrated-integrated-photonic-processor-prepares-and-measures-arbitrary-t--f41a0c8f645b\",\n    \"claim-the-photonic-variational-eigensolver-experimentally-recovered-the-he-h-bond-diss--5898494f9b1f\",\n    \"claim-nisq-devices-are-best-understood-as-experimental-tools-for-exploring-many-body-q--fde7f9646dbb\",\n    \"claim-random-quantum-circuits-become-exponentially-harder-to-simulate-classically-as-q--f7cd81f80f31\",\n    \"claim-the-demonstrated-speedup-is-specific-to-random-circuit-sampling-and-does-not-rem--47d4f349751e\"\n  ],\n  \"sections\": [\n    {\n      \"body\": \"The QML source allows deep quantum learning to use quantum annealers, programmable photonic circuits, and quantum Boltzmann machines rather than requiring a large universal quantum computer. This connects to the photonic VQE experiment, which demonstrates a task-specific integrated photonic processor, and to NISQ framing that near-term devices are best understood as experimental tools and stepping stones.\",\n      \"heading\": \"Beyond universal fault-tolerant machines\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"body\": \"Quantum Boltzmann machine training claims quadratic improvements in thermalization, sampling, and data access under quantum-coherent or qRAM assumptions. Random-circuit sampling and photonic expectation estimation are different tasks, but they share a broader theme: near-term platforms may be evaluated by how well they produce, sample, or measure quantum distributions under constrained coherence.\",\n      \"heading\": \"Sampling and thermalization as shared primitives\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"body\": \"The evidence supports special-purpose platforms as plausible testbeds, not settled replacements for universal fault-tolerant computation. Their value depends on benchmarked performance against classical methods and on whether hardware-specific advantages survive realistic noise and access assumptions.\",\n      \"heading\": \"Open comparison problem\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"source-05-quantum-machine-learning--a91f0184eb29\",\n    \"source-04-a-variational-eigenvalue-solver-on-a-photonic-quantum-processor--4678297edf5b\",\n    \"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\",\n    \"source-02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor--f98990eb22d8\"\n  ],\n  \"structure_type\": \"wiki\",\n  \"title\": \"Special-purpose quantum platforms broaden the near-term learning landscape\",\n  \"topic_id\": \"topic-special-purpose-platforms-for-near-term-quantum-learning\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
